# Security

## Baseline

Treat every external input as untrusted. Defense in depth: authentication, authorization, validation, DB constraints, safe logging, rate limiting, audit logging.

## Authentication

- Hash passwords with Argon2id; never encrypt or log credentials.
- Short-lived access tokens; longer refresh tokens; separate secrets.
- Store refresh tokens hashed in `auth_sessions`.
- Rotate refresh tokens; revoke families on reuse when supported.
- OTP, reset, and magic-link tokens: random, hashed at rest, single-use, expiring.
- Avoid account enumeration in auth error messages.
- Issue encrypted bearer envelopes; decrypt via `EncryptedBearerTokenMiddleware` before `JwtAuthGuard`.

## Authorization

Authentication is not authorization. Verify active account, required role/permission, resource policy, and allowed state transitions on protected actions.

Prefer role/permission decorators and central guards over scattered role checks.

Typical authenticated stack: `ApiKeyGuard` → `JwtAuthGuard` → `RolesGuard` (when roles apply).

Built-in roles: `SUPER_ADMIN` | `ADMIN` | `USER`.

## Validation

```ts
new ValidationPipe({
  whitelist: true,
  forbidNonWhitelisted: true,
  transform: true,
})
```

Set max lengths; validate UUIDs, emails, enums; reject server-managed fields from clients.

## HTTP security

- Helmet, strict CORS allowlist, HTTPS in production.
- Rate limits on auth, password reset, and sensitive endpoints.
- Request body size limits.

## Injection protection

- Parameterized Drizzle queries only.
- Allowlist sort/filter fields.

## Mass assignment

Map DTO fields explicitly in repositories/services; never pass raw DTOs to persistence.

## Secrets

- Never commit `.env`.
- Fail startup on missing required secrets.
- Separate secrets per environment; rotate on compromise.

## Logging

Include request/correlation ID, route, status, duration, actor when safe. Redact authorization headers, cookies, passwords, tokens, OTPs.

## Audit logs

Append-only audit for role changes, auth security events, sensitive data changes. Include actor, action, target, timestamp, safe metadata.

## Error responses

Stable shape and codes; no stack traces, SQL text, or internal hostnames.

## Dependency security

Commit lockfile; review new dependencies; run `pnpm audit` / `pnpm audit:security` in CI. Do not suppress advisories with audit-level tricks.
